hexagon: an environment switch for the FWHT form of the KV cache rotation
Fold-into: memory/0006-hexagon-run-the-kv-cache-rotation-as-a-fast-walsh-hadamard-transform.patch

The defect

patches/memory/0006 sends each rotation of a quantized KV cache that
ggml_hexagon_is_fwht accepts (a MUL_MAT with the hint
GGML_HINT_SRC0_IS_HADAMARD) to the DSP op HTP_OP_FWHT. No switch keeps
such a rotation as HTP_OP_MUL_MAT. Thus a comparison of the two forms on
the phone must use two library sets.

The change

GGML_HEXAGON_FWHT=0 keeps each such rotation as HTP_OP_MUL_MAT. The preset
value 1 keeps the behavior of patches/memory/0006. With the value 0, the
backend writes the log line "ggml-hex: the KV cache rotation stays MUL_MAT
(GGML_HEXAGON_FWHT=0)" when it starts.

The results

On the phone (HTP0, 2026-09-24), the stage bench-kv (tools/stages/bench-kv)
used the libraries of the series of e8a3a07 with this patch. Each of the
116 runs of llama-bench and memprobe (58 for the 4B Q8_0 and 58 for the 2B
Q8_0) gave the exit code 0. In the profile runs with the value 0 (Q8_0 K
and V, variant C), no rotation was an HTP_OP_FWHT op, and each of the 18
logs of variant C has the log line of the switch. With the preset value
(variant B), each of the 32 rotations of a decode token of the 4B was an
HTP_OP_FWHT op.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

